# Files that live in the repo but must never be served.
# Anything in the project root is public by default on a static host, so this
# list is what stands between an internal document and a downloadable one.
# It is not the same list as .gitignore: everything here is committed on
# purpose, it just has no business being on the domain.

# Internal notes and local tooling config.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# The full TTFs are the source for regenerating img/og-image.png. The site
# itself only loads the subset woff2 files.
fonts/*.ttf
fonts/*.otf

# Licensed for artwork, not for serving: the face the division lockups are set
# in. The site ships the traced outlines (img/wordmark-*.svg), never the font.
fonts/brandon-grotesque-light.ttf

# Brand originals, 4MB between them. _tools/build-brand-assets.py turns these
# into everything the site actually loads; none is referenced by a page.
# "Silver logo.png" is the brushed-metal render — the source of the /mark
# plate and the share card, kept because the outputs are cut from it.
img/Logo.png
img/Text logo.png
img/Silver logo.png

# Build scripts, and the render spec, which is an internal brief.
_tools/

# Generated as the standing check on the division lockups — the site uses the
# real img/wordmark.svg for TECH, never this re-set copy of it. Git ignores it
# too; this entry is for the case where a build has just run.
img/wordmark-tech.svg
